    {
      "id": "vocabulary",
      "status": "source-backed",
      "interpretation": "Package, event, port and directed interface vocabulary used to formalize the input.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "WORKSHOP",
          "startLine": 4,
          "endLine": 4,
          "quote": "The naming, packaging and reusable SysML vocabulary in this exercise may be chosen by the model author without changing the source facts. Group all declarations under PumpStationStudy. Use Command ports carrying StartRequest and a CommandExchange interface with a directed flow from source to target. The stop, fault and reset events are motor behavior triggers; no station routing for these events is specified."
        },
        {
          "source": "ARCH",
          "startLine": 5,
          "endLine": 5,
          "quote": "Each motor has operating states stopped, running and tripped; entry selects stopped. StartRequest changes stopped to running, StopRequest changes running to stopped, FaultNotice changes running to tripped, and ResetRequest changes tripped to stopped. These event-triggered transitions specify behavior; they do not demonstrate execution."
        }
      ],
